{{also|Swan|SWAN|ꓢꓪꓮꓠꓸ}}
==English==
{{wp}}
[[Image:Schwan1 db.jpg|250px|thumb|[[mute swan|Mute swan]] ({{taxfmt|Cygnus olor|species}})]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/swɒn/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/swɑn/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-swan.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒn|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:swan|tree=+}}
From {{inh|en|enm|swan}}, from {{inh|en|ang|swan}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*swan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*swanaz|t=swan|lit=the singing bird}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro||*swonh₂-}}/{{m|ine-pro|*swenh₂-||to sing, make sound}}.

Cognate with {{cog|fy|swan}}, {{cog|nds|Swaan}}, {{m|nds|swan}}, {{cog|nl|zwaan}}, {{cog|de|Schwan}}, {{cog|da|svane}}, {{cog|no|svane}}, {{cog|sv|svan}}. Related also to {{cog|ang|ġeswin|t=melody, song}}, {{cog|ang|swinsian|t=to make melody}}.

Further cognates include (possibly) {{cog|ru|звон|t=ring, chime}}; {{cog|la|sonus|t=sound}}, {{cog|sa|स्वन्|t=sound}}.
{{doublet|en|sound}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|s|*}}

# {{senseid|en|Q34384}}Any of various species of large, long-necked [[waterfowl]], of genus {{taxfmt|Cygnus|genus}} (bird family: {{taxfmt|Anatidae|family}}), most of which have white plumage.
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} One whose grace etc. suggests a swan.
# {{lb|en|heraldiccharge}} This bird used as a [[heraldry|heraldic]] charge, sometimes with a [[crown]] around its [[neck]] (e. g. the arms of [[Buckinghamshire]]).

