===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|swymmen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|swimman|t=to swim, float}} (class III strong verb; past tense ''swamm'', past participle ''geswummen''), from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*swimman}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*swimmaną|t=to swim}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*swem(bʰ)-|t=to be unsteady, move, swim}}.
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|frr|sweem}}, {{m|frr|swome}}, {{m|frr|swume}}, {{m|frr|swumi}}, {{m|frr|swumme}}, {{m|frr|swääm|t=to swim}}, {{cog|stq,fy|swimme|t=to swim}}, {{cog|nl|zwemmen|t=to swim}}, {{cog|de|schwimmen|t=to swim}}, {{cog|li|schwämme}}, {{m|li|zwömme|t=to swim}}, {{cog|nds|swimmen|t=to swim}}, {{cog|lb|schwammen|t=to swim}}, {{cog|wym|švymma}}, {{m|wym|śwyma}}, {{m|wym|śwymma|t=to swim}}, {{cog|yi|שווימען|t=to swim}}, {{cog|da,nb|svømme|t=to swim}}, {{cog|fo|svimja|t=to swim}}, {{cog|nrn|suma|t=to swim}}, {{cog|nn|svemja}}, {{m|nn|svemje}}, {{m|nn|svømma}}, {{m|nn|svømme}}, {{m|nn|symja}}, {{m|nn|symje|t=to swim}}, {{cog|sv|simma|t=to swim}}.
