====Verb====
{{en-verb|+|+|+,~|+,~en<l:archaic>}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To emit sweat.
#: {{syn|en|perspire}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cause to excrete moisture through skin.
## To cause to perspire.
##: {{ux|en|His physicians attempted to '''sweat''' him by most powerful sudorifics.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|informal}} To work hard.
#: {{syn|en|slave|slog}}
#: {{ux|en|I've been '''sweating''' over my essay all day.}}
## {{lb|en|video games}} To be extremely [[dedicated]] to winning a game; to play [[competitively]].
##: {{syn|en|tryhard}}
##: {{ux|en|There's no way we can win. These guys are '''sweating''' so hard.}}
##* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.washingtonpost.com/video-games/2022/05/27/skill-based-matchmaking/|work=The Washington Post|passage=With skill-based matchmaking, he wrote, "you have to '''sweat''' 100 percent of the time." They contend their audiences want to see them pull off amazing victories, not struggle endlessly against other top players.|title=Video game developers want fair online games. Some players really don’t.|date=2022-05-27|author=Ethan Davison}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} To extract money, labour, etc. from, by [[exaction]] or [[oppression]].
#: {{syn|en|bleed}}
#: {{ux|en|to '''sweat''' a spendthrift}}
#: {{ux|en|to '''sweat''' labourers}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 September 7|author=Tom Allett|title=At the cutting edge of NR's track work|journal=RAIL|issue=965|page=40|text="I've predicted it will last 32 years. The last overhaul we will do on it is at 24 years, but we tend to '''sweat''' the asset at Network Rail and try and save a bit of money, so I've estimated 32 years."}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|informal}} To worry.
#: {{syn|en|fret|worry}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} To worry about (something). {{defdate|from 20th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|[[don't sweat it|Don't '''sweat''' it]]!}}
#: {{ux|en|to [[sweat the small stuff|'''sweat''' the small stuff]]}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Brooks Barnes|title=Studios battle to save Narnia|journal=The New York Times|date=5 Dec 2010
|passage=There are few matters studio executives '''sweat''' more than maintaining their franchises.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To emit, in the manner of sweat.
