#* {{quote-book|en|year=1954|author=W. E. Blackhurst|title=Riders of the Flood|page=27
|passage=Nothing to it but clearing out underbrush and limbs so teams can get to the logs. {{...}} If anyone asks, just tell him you've '''swamped''' roads ever since you was big enough to lift a hatchet.}}
